From: Avocado Linux <info@avocadolinux.org>
Subject: [PATCH] main.h: include the headers that declare the map and ble_hrc menus

Two profile blocks include the wrong header, so with the profile enabled the
functions main.c calls are never declared:

  BTAPP_MAP_ENABLE     -> "ctn.h"      (map_menu_display/_handle are in map.h)
  BTAPP_BLE_HRC_ENABLE -> "app_ble.h"  (ble_hrc_menu_* are in app_ble_hrc.h)

Both profiles are enabled by the Makefile, so main.c compiled only because C
let an undeclared call through with a warning. GCC 14 made
-Wimplicit-function-declaration an error, so it now fails:

  main.c:363:17: error: implicit declaration of function 'map_menu_display';
  did you mean 'sap_menu_display'?
  main.c:424:17: error: implicit declaration of function 'ble_hrc_menu_display';
  did you mean 'ble_htp_menu_display'?

Include the right headers. Every other block already follows this convention
- the adjacent BTAPP_BLE_HTP_ENABLE block includes "app_ble_htp.h" - and the
#else stubs stay untouched for builds with the profiles off.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor fork, rubikpi-ai/rubikpi_bt_bsa_demo]
---
--- a/src/linux/main/include/main.h
+++ b/src/linux/main/include/main.h
@@ -153,7 +153,7 @@
 #endif
 
 #ifdef BTAPP_MAP_ENABLE
-#include "ctn.h"
+#include "map.h"
 #else
 void map_menu_display(void)
 {
@@ -391,7 +391,7 @@
 #endif
 
 #ifdef BTAPP_BLE_HRC_ENABLE
-#include "app_ble.h"
+#include "app_ble_hrc.h"
 #else
 void ble_hrc_menu_display(void)
 {
